---
import Prose from "../layouts/Prose.astro";
import { OWN_LICENCE } from "../lib/licence";
import { repo } from "../lib/site";

const mcp = "https://charityevals.org/mcp";
const cursorConfig = `{
  "mcpServers": {
    "charityevals": { "url": "${mcp}" }
  }
}`;
// The server's tools (worker/), one line each.
const tools = [
  ["search_charities(query, cause?)", "find charities and their model ids"],
  ["get_model(id)", "a model's rows, with value, range, source and explanation"],
  ["run_model(id, values?)", "recompute one model with your values"],
  ["compare(ids, values?)", "several models side by side, with your values"],
  ["rank(cause?, values?, limit?)", "every charity ranked, with your values"],
  ["list_assumptions()", "the values you can change and the value sets"],
];
const prompts = [
  "Rank the global health charities at a 1% discount rate.",
  "Compare GiveDirectly and Helen Keller Intl under the AI-concerned value set.",
  "Explain what drives the Against Malaria Foundation's result, and which input matters most.",
];
// The static files (src/pages/data/), built from the same library as the pages.
const files = [
  ["/data/charities.json", "JSON", "every charity"],
  ["/data/models.json", "JSON", "one entry per model: charity, evaluator, cause, headline, range, licence, links"],
  ["/data/models/<id>.json", "JSON", "one full model: every row, its computed value, headline and range"],
  ["/data/assumptions.json", "JSON", "the values you can change, with ranges, and the value sets"],
  ["/data/facts.json", "JSON", "the shared data every model reads"],
  ["/data/results.csv", "CSV", "one row per model"],
  ["/data/library.json", "JSON", "all the inputs above in one file, to recompute any model"],
];
---

<Prose title="Use with AI" active="ai" description="Ask an AI assistant to rank, compare or explain charities with your own values, through our MCP server, plain-text files or open data.">
  <p class="dek">Ask an AI assistant to rank, compare or explain the models here, with your own values. Its answers are estimates, not advice.</p>

  <h2>Connect the MCP server</h2>
  <p>Server URL: <code>{mcp}</code>. No sign-in.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Claude</strong> (claude.ai and Claude Desktop): Customize › Connectors › + Add › Add custom connector. Name it charityevals, paste the URL, choose No sign in, then Add. On Team and Enterprise, an owner adds it under Organization settings › Connectors. <a href="https://support.claude.com/en/articles/11175166-getting-started-with-custom-connectors-using-remote-mcp">Anthropic's guide</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Claude Code</strong>: <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/mcp">guide</a>
      <pre class="code"><code>claude mcp add --transport http charityevals {mcp}</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>ChatGPT</strong> (on the web): open <a href="https://chatgpt.com/plugins">Plugins</a>, select + › Add custom MCP server, paste the URL under Connection, choose No authentication, confirm, then Create as a plugin and install it. <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/custom-mcp-server">OpenAI's guide</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cursor</strong>: add this to <code>~/.cursor/mcp.json</code>, or to <code>.cursor/mcp.json</code> in a project. <a href="https://cursor.com/docs/context/mcp">Cursor's guide</a>
      <pre class="code"><code>{cursorConfig}</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Other clients</strong>: any that connects to remote MCP servers over Streamable HTTP. Use the URL above.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Tools</h3>
  <ul>
    {tools.map(([name, does]) => <li><code>{name}</code>: {does}</li>)}
  </ul>
  <p><code>values</code> maps an assumption id to a number, or names a value set: <code>{"{ \"set\": \"ai-concerned\" }"}</code>.</p>

  <h3>Try</h3>
  <ul>
    {prompts.map((p) => <li>“{p}”</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>Without setup</h2>
  <p>
    Give any AI chat this link: <a href="/llms-full.txt"><code>charityevals.org/llms-full.txt</code></a>. It has every charity's models, headline, range, main drivers and sources as plain text. <a href="/llms.txt"><code>/llms.txt</code></a> is a shorter map of the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Data files</h2>
  <table class="files">
    <tbody>
      {files.map(([path, format, holds]) => (
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">{path.includes("<") ? <code>{path}</code> : <a href={path}><code>{path}</code></a>}</th>
          <td class="muted">{format}</td>
          <td>{holds}</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Results are years of healthy life per $1,000 at the default values. The model files are also in the <a href={repo}>repository</a>.</p>

  <h2>Share a view</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>?set=&lt;id&gt;</code> picks a value set, as in <a href="/?set=ai-concerned"><code>/?set=ai-concerned</code></a>.</li>
    <li>
      <code>?values=&lt;id&gt;:&lt;number&gt;,…</code> sets single values, written as in <code>/data/assumptions.json</code> (0.01 is 1%), as in <a href="/?values=discount_rate:0.01"><code>/?values=discount_rate:0.01</code></a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>The Copy link button writes your current values into a link.</p>

  <h2>Reuse</h2>
  <p>
    Our own models, write-ups and data are <a href={OWN_LICENCE.url}>{OWN_LICENCE.name}</a>: credit {OWN_LICENCE.attribution}. Models rebuilt from an evaluator's analysis keep that evaluator's terms. Every data file and tool answer names its licence. The code is MIT. See the <a href="/terms">terms</a>.
  </p>
</Prose>

<style>
  .dek {
    font-size: 19px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: 17px;
    margin: var(--s5) 0 var(--s2);
  }
  .code {
    margin: var(--s2) 0 0;
    padding: var(--s3);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--paper-2);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .code code {
    background: none;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .files {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .files th,
  .files td {
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    padding: var(--s2) var(--s3) var(--s2) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .files th {
    font-weight: 400;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .files th {
      white-space: normal;
      word-break: break-all;
    }
  }
</style>
